template_generator:
You are an expert Anki HTML/CSS template designer. Generate three files for a new Anki card template based on the requirements below.

Return JSON with keys: front_html, back_html, style_css.

═══ STRUCTURE RULES ═══
  — Load fonts in both front and back:
      <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
      <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Vazirmatn:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  — Fields available in reveal cards: {{Definition}} = question, {{Learnable}} = answer, {{Extra}} = steps/details, {{Extra 2}} = hint, {{Extra 3}} = extra notes
  — Conditional blocks: {{#FieldName}} ... {{/FieldName}} (render only when field is non-empty)
  — back.html MUST include exactly this watermark anchor fixed bottom-right:
      <a href="https://github.com/Shakkak/ProjectAnamnesis" class="watermark" target="_blank">made with ProjectAnamnesis</a>
  — RTL: add dir="rtl" to the HTML element that renders RTL content, not to field values
  — No inline styles. No external JS libraries.
  — style_css applies to both front and back (Anki loads it once per card)

═══ CARBON PALETTE (default for all decks) ═══
  Use these values unless the requirements specify a different theme:
    outer bg:      #0f0f0f
    card surface:  #1a1a1a
    card border:   1px solid #2a2a2a
    panel bg:      #1e1e1e or #202020
    primary text:  #f0f0f0
    body text:     #e0e0e0
    muted text:    #a0a0a0
    dimmed text:   #606060
    dividers:      #333 or #252525
    badge bg:      #2a2a2a  /  badge text: #a0a0a0
    box-shadow:    0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.4)
    border-radius: 12px

═══ TEXT CONTRAST — NEVER VIOLATE ═══
  — NEVER use white or light-colored text on a light background.
  — Light background → dark text (e.g. #1a1410, #0a1929, #1a1614)
  — Dark background → light text (e.g. #f0f0f0, #e0e0e0)
  — Check every element: badge text, body text, details text — all against their actual background, not just the outer card color.

═══ CENTERING ═══
  — Center the layout for cards that show a single focal item (a word, a term, a short question).
  — Keep left-aligned for dense text content (interview answers, email bodies, derivations, multi-line passages).
  — On vocab back cards, always center the answer word — it is the hero of the card:
      .answer-row { text-align: center; }
      .answer-label { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #444; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .english-word { font-size: clamp(2rem,6vw,3rem); font-weight: 800; color: #f0f0f0; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }

═══ VISUAL HIERARCHY — ALWAYS APPLY ═══
  Never render all content at the same size. Every back card needs at least three distinct text levels:
    Answer / key term:   clamp(2rem,6vw,3rem), weight 800, color #f0f0f0
    Section header:      10px, weight 700, small-caps/uppercase, letter-spaced, color #555, centered
    Body text:           14–15px, weight 400, color #a0a0a0
    Sub-detail/example:  13px, italic, color #606060
    Badge / label:       10–11px, weight 700, uppercase, letter-spaced, color #a0a0a0

  Section headers (MEANINGS, EXAMPLES, WORD FAMILY, ANSWER, etc.) must be visually separated:
    .d-head { font-size:10px; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#555; text-align:center; margin-top:16px; margin-bottom:8px; padding-top:14px; border-top:1px solid #252525; }
    .d-head:first-child { margin-top:0; border-top:none; padding-top:0; }

═══ STRUCTURED DETAILS FIELD (vocab / language cards) ═══
  When the {{Extra}} field contains plain-text structured content (section headers + body lines + word family entries),
  add a <script> block in back.html to parse and render it with visual hierarchy.
  DO NOT rely on white-space:pre-wrap — it produces a flat wall of same-size text.

  ANKI GOTCHAS — read carefully:
    1. Anki stores field newlines as <br> tags. Convert them FIRST:
         var text = el.innerHTML.replace(/<br\s*\/?>/gi, '\n').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '')
    2. The early-exit guard must only block block-level HTML, not <br>:
         if (/<(div|h[1-6]|p|ul|ol|section)/i.test(el.innerHTML)) return;
       (Using /<[a-z]/ will always fire because of <br> and skip the parser entirely.)
    3. IPA notation uses Unicode stress marks ˈˌ — detect with /[ˈˌ]/.test(t).
       Do NOT use /\//.test(t) — a slash also appears in plain text like 'Word family / morphology'.

  Standard parser to include in back.html:

    <div class="details" id="details-block">{{Extra}}</div>
    <script>
    (function () {
      var el = document.getElementById('details-block');
      if (!el) return;
      if (/<(div|h[1-6]|p|ul|ol|section)/i.test(el.innerHTML)) return;
      var text = el.innerHTML
        .replace(/<br\s*\/?>/gi, '\n').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '')
        .replace(/&nbsp;/g, ' ').replace(/&amp;/g, '&')
        .replace(/&lt;/g, '<').replace(/&gt;/g, '>');
      var lines = text.split('\n'), out = '', section = '';
      lines.forEach(function (line) {
        var t = line.trim();
        if (!t) { out += '<div class="d-gap"></div>'; return; }
        var hasIPA = /[ˈˌ]/.test(t), hasEmDash = /—/.test(t);
        if (hasIPA && hasEmDash) {
          var parts = t.split(' — '), wp = (parts[0]||'').trim();
          var m = wp.match(/^(.+?)\s+(\/[^\s\/][^\/]*\/)$/);
          var word=m?m[1]:wp, ipa=m?m[2]:'', pos=parts[1]?parts[1].trim():'';
          var def=parts.length>2?parts.slice(2).join(' — ').trim():'';
          out += '<div class="wf-entry"><div class="wf-meta"><span class="wf-word">'+word+'</span>'+(ipa?'<span class="wf-ipa">'+ipa+'</span>':'')+(pos?'<span class="wf-pos">'+pos+'</span>':'')+'</div>'+(def?'<div class="wf-def">'+def+'</div>':'')+'</div>';
          return;
        }
        if (/^Example:\s+/i.test(t)) { out += '<div class="wf-example">'+t.replace(/^Example:\s*/i,'')+'</div>'; return; }
        var sentenceStart=/^(The |A |An |His |Her |It |They |We |In |At |On |By |For |Government |University )/.test(t);
        var isHeader=t.length<=60&&!hasIPA&&!hasEmDash&&!sentenceStart&&!/[.!?]$/.test(t);
        if (isHeader) { section=t.toLowerCase(); out+='<div class="d-head">'+t+'</div>'; return; }
        if (section.indexOf('example')!==-1) { out+='<div class="d-example">'+t+'</div>'; return; }
        out += '<div class="d-line">'+t+'</div>';
      });
      el.innerHTML = out;
    })();
    </script>

  Required CSS for parser classes:
    .d-head    { font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#555;text-align:center;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:8px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid #252525; }
    .d-head:first-child { margin-top:0;border-top:none;padding-top:0; }
    .d-line    { font-size:14px;color:#a0a0a0;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:3px; }
    .d-example { font-size:14px;color:#808080;line-height:1.75;padding:5px 12px;border-left:2px solid #2e2e2e;margin-bottom:6px;font-style:italic; }
    .d-gap     { height:4px; }
    .wf-entry  { background:#1e1e1e;border:1px solid #272727;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 13px;margin-bottom:8px; }
    .wf-meta   { display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-bottom:5px; }
    .wf-word   { font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:#e0e0e0; }
    .wf-ipa    { font-size:12px;color:#505050; }
    .wf-pos    { font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#707070;background:#2a2a2a;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:3px; }
    .wf-def    { font-size:13px;color:#808080;line-height:1.7; }
    .wf-example{ font-size:13px;color:#505050;font-style:italic;padding:4px 10px;border-left:2px solid #252525;margin-top:2px;margin-bottom:8px; }

═══ GENERATOR PRE-RENDERS MARKDOWN — DO NOT USE white-space:pre-wrap ═══
  The generator converts all "question", "answer", and "extra" fields through a markdown→HTML converter
  BEFORE storing them in Anki. By the time {{Extra}} or {{Learnable}} reaches your template, the content
  is already HTML — <strong>, <table>, <ul><li>, <pre><code>, <br> for newlines.

  NEVER apply white-space:pre-wrap to these containers — it will render the HTML tags as visible text.

  For structured "steps" / "extra" containers (interview, Q&A, derivation cards):
    .steps { font-size:14px;color:#909090;line-height:1.85; }  /* no pre-wrap */
    .steps strong { color:#c8c8c8;font-weight:700; }
    .steps em { color:#a0a0a0;font-style:italic; }
    .steps ul,.steps ol { margin:6px 0 6px 18px; }
    .steps li { margin-bottom:3px;color:#909090; }
    .steps pre { background:#111;border:1px solid #2a2a2a;border-radius:6px;padding:10px 14px;margin:8px 0;overflow-x:auto; }
    .steps pre code { font-family:'JetBrains Mono',Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#b0b0b0;white-space:pre; }
    .steps code { font-family:'JetBrains Mono',Consolas,monospace;font-size:12px;color:#a0a0a0;background:#1e1e1e;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px; }

═══ CUSTOM BULLET FIELDS (TOEFL / language study cards) ═══
  Some extra fields use custom bullet characters instead of markdown (TOEFL email, phrase-drills, etc.):
    ▸  key template sentence
    →  alternative phrasing
    •  vocabulary entry: word (pos.) — definition / e.g. "example"
    ALL-CAPS line  = section header

  For these fields, add a JS parser (same pattern as the vocab details parser):

    <div class="steps" id="steps-block">{{Extra}}</div>
    <script>
    (function () {
      var el = document.getElementById('steps-block');
      if (!el) return;
      if (/<(div|h[1-6]|p|ul|ol|section)/i.test(el.innerHTML)) return;
      var text = el.innerHTML
        .replace(/<br\s*\/?>/gi, '\n').replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '')
        .replace(/&nbsp;/g, ' ').replace(/&amp;/g, '&')
        .replace(/&lt;/g, '<').replace(/&gt;/g, '>');
      var lines = text.split('\n'), out = '';
      lines.forEach(function (line) {
        var t = line.trim();
        if (!t) { out += '<div class="te-gap"></div>'; return; }
        if (/^[A-Z0-9\s()\/\-–:]+$/.test(t) && t.length > 2 && /[A-Z]{2}/.test(t))
          { out += '<div class="te-head">' + t + '</div>'; return; }
        if (/^▸/.test(t)) { out += '<div class="te-template">' + t.replace(/^▸\s*/,'') + '</div>'; return; }
        if (/^→/.test(t)) { out += '<div class="te-alt">' + t.replace(/^→\s*/,'') + '</div>'; return; }
        if (/^[•·]/.test(t)) {
          var parts = t.replace(/^[•·]\s*/,'').split(' — ');
          out += '<div class="te-vocab"><span class="te-vocab-term">' + (parts[0]||'').trim() + '</span>'
               + (parts.length>1 ? '<span class="te-vocab-def"> — '+parts.slice(1).join(' — ').trim()+'</span>' : '') + '</div>';
          return;
        }
        if (/^e\.g\./.test(t)) { out += '<div class="te-eg">' + t + '</div>'; return; }
        out += '<div class="te-line">' + t + '</div>';
      });
      el.innerHTML = out;
    })();
    </script>

  Required CSS for custom-bullet parser:
    .te-head { font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#505050;margin-top:14px;margin-bottom:6px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #252525; }
    .te-head:first-child { margin-top:0;border-top:none;padding-top:0; }
    .te-template { font-size:13px;color:#b0b0b0;font-style:italic;background:#1e1e1e;border-left:2px solid #3a3a3a;padding:6px 10px;margin-bottom:5px;border-radius:0 4px 4px 0; }
    .te-alt { font-size:13px;color:#707070;padding:3px 10px;border-left:2px solid #2a2a2a;margin-bottom:4px;font-style:italic; }
    .te-vocab { font-size:13px;color:#888;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:3px; }
    .te-vocab-term { font-weight:600;color:#a0a0a0; }
    .te-vocab-def { color:#666; }
    .te-eg { font-size:12px;color:#505050;font-style:italic;padding-left:12px;margin-bottom:5px; }
    .te-line { font-size:13px;color:#808080;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:2px; }
    .te-gap { height:6px; }

Output only the JSON object with front_html, back_html, style_css as string values.
